  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n // Fixed in release-3.6: xxxx\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n // CWE-???\n+* ISO15765 and ISO10681 dissectors corrupt memory and Wireshark may crash wsbuglink:18839[].\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -48,6 +49,30 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark keeps banging out random chords on your piano and yelling “LIPS LIKE SUGUAR, SUGAR KISSES” because it was funny that one time at a party.\n \n+* UTF-8 characters end up escaped in PSML output wsbuglink:10445[].\n+\n+* The intelligent scroll bar or minimap is not predictable on locating and scrolling wsbuglink:13989[].\n+\n+* If you mark (or unmark) the currently-selected frame, the packet details still say it's not marked (or it is marked) wsbuglink:14330[].\n+\n+* Sorting Packet Loss Column is not sorting correct wsbuglink:16785[].\n+\n+* SIP TCP decoding regression from Wireshark 1.99.0 to 3.6.8 wsbuglink:18411[].\n+\n+* ChmodBPF not working on macOS Ventura 13.1 wsbuglink:18734[].\n+\n+* Symbolic links to packages in macOS dmg can't be double-clicked to install on macOS 13.2 wsbuglink:18830[].\n+\n+* Potential memory leak in tshark.c wsbuglink:18837[].\n+\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-02-05-7303.pcap wsbuglink:18842[].\n+\n+* f5fileinfo: Hardware platforms missing descriptions wsbuglink:18848[].\n+\n+* The lines in the intelligent scrollbar are off by one wsbuglink:18850[].\n+\n+* TECMP dissector shows the wrong Voltage in Vendor Data wsbuglink:18871[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n@@ -61,9 +86,33 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.6.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n+// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.6.11.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+DHCP\n+ERF\n+F5 Ethernet trailer\n+GMR-1 RR\n+GSM SMS\n+Gryphon\n+H.450\n+ISO 10681\n+ISO 15765\n+NAS-5GS\n+NR RRC\n+NS Trace\n+OptoMMP\n+PDCP-LTE\n+QSIG\n+ROHC\n+RSVP\n+RTCP\n+SCTP\n+SIP\n+TCP\n+TECMP\n+TWAMP\n+UMTS RLC\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
